c EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis c x right parenthesis equals x minus 8\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis StartFraction 2 c Over c EndFraction right parenthesis equals StartFraction 2 Over c EndFraction minus 8\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals StartFraction 2 Over c EndFraction minus 8\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Since it’s given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis equals 35\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn></math>, substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"35 equals StartFraction 2 Over c EndFraction minus 8\"><mn>35</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> to both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"43 equals StartFraction 2 Over c EndFraction\"><mn>43</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"43 c equals 2\"><mn>43</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"43\"><mn>43</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c equals two forty thirds\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>43</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that 2/43, .0465, 0.046, and 0.047 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","externalid":"f268654f-d968-4474-abc8-911195b0c902","correct_answer":[".0465","2/43"]},"createDate":1755117017726,"updateDate":1755117017726}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017726, 1755117017726),
