aded region shown represents the solutions to an inequality, an ordered pair <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a solution to the inequality if it's represented by a point in the shaded region. Of the given choices, only <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 6 comma negative 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is represented by a point in the shaded region. Therefore, the ordered pair <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 6 comma negative 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is a solution to this inequality.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","externalid":"efb5e6bb-bcbd-403b-9d21-1e079c979104","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554988,"updateDate":1743430554988}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554988, 1743430554988),
