In the equation above, <span class=\"italic\">a</span> and <span class=\"italic\">b</span> are constants and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than a, which is less than b\"></span>. Which of the following could represent the graph of the equation in the <span class=\"italic \">xy</span>-plane?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">&nbsp;<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The answer choice presents the graph of a line in the x y-plane. The number 1 is indicated on both axes. The line slants downward and to the right, crossing the y axis at 1, and crossing the x axis at 1.\" width=\"82\" height=\"89\"></p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">&nbsp;<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The answer choice presents the graph of a line in the x y-plane. The number 1 is indicated on both axes. The line slants downward and to the right, crossing the x axis at negative 1, and crossing the y axis at negative 1.\" width=\"82\" height=\"89\"></p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">&nbsp;<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The answer choice presents the graph of a line in the x y-plane. The number 1 is indicated on both axes. The line slants downward and to the right, crossing the y axis at 1, and crossing the x axis at 2.\" width=\"82\" height=\"89\"></p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">&nbsp;<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The answer choice presents the graph of a line in the x y-plane. The number 1 is indicated on both axes. The line slants downward and to the right, crossing the y axis at 1, and crossing the x axis at 0 point 5.\" width=\"82\" height=\"89\"></p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. The given equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, x plus b y, equals b\"></span> can be rewritten in slope-intercept form, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, m x plus k\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">m</span> represents the slope of the line represented by the equation, and <span class=\"italic\">k</span> represents the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of the line. Subtracting <span class=\"italic\">ax</span> from both sides of the equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"b y equals, negative a, x plus b\"></span>, and dividing both sides of this equation by <span class=\"italic\">b</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, the negative of the fraction a over b, end fraction, times x, plus, the fraction b over b, end fraction\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, the negative of the fraction a over b, end fraction, times x, plus 1\"></span>. With the equation now in slope-intercept form, it shows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"k equals 1\"></span>, which means the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept is 1. It&rsquo;s given that <span class=\"italic\">a</span> and <span class=\"italic\">b</span> are both greater than 0 (positive) and that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a is less than b\"></span>. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"m equals, the negative of the fraction a over b\"></span>, the slope of the line must be a value between <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABcAAAAYCAYAAAARfGZ1AAAACXBIWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAABGJhU0UAAAAMyZLetQAAAFhJREFUeNpjYKAMtADxNiB+DsT/oXyqgS9AfAyIp9LCcCYkNtUNZyDWcBEiMBu5hv8nAoeQa7gLEViMXMNpGuYjy/AQJAwyfA0SnyquxYVHwSgYBaOAJgAAQ7AqWC3zu8cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=\" alt=\"negative 1\"></span> and 0. Choice C is the only graph of a line that has a <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-value of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept that is 1 and a slope that is between <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABcAAAAYCAYAAAARfGZ1AAAACXBIWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAABGJhU0UAAAAMyZLetQAAAFhJREFUeNpjYKAMtADxNiB+DsT/oXyqgS9AfAyIp9LCcCYkNtUNZyDWcBEiMBu5hv8nAoeQa7gLEViMXMNpGuYjy/AQJAwyfA0SnyquxYVHwSgYBaOAJgAAQ7AqWC3zu8cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=\" alt=\"negative 1\"></span> and 0.<p>Choices A, B, and D are incorrect because the slopes of the lines in these graphs aren&rsquo;t between <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABcAAAAYCAYAAAARfGZ1AAAACXBIWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAABGJhU0UAAAAMyZLetQAAAFhJREFUeNpjYKAMtADxNiB+DsT/oXyqgS9AfAyIp9LCcCYkNtUNZyDWcBEiMBu5hv8nAoeQa7gLEViMXMNpGuYjy/AQJAwyfA0SnyquxYVHwSgYBaOAJgAAQ7AqWC3zu8cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=\" alt=\"negative 1\"></span> and 0.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959626,"updateDate":1691007959626}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959626, 1691007959626),
    ($SATQ$0bd33265$SATQ$, $SATQ$e47cdf24-1ef9-4aa4-bc46-70b25da6e45e$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The equation&nbsp;<math alttext="h equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>273.15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math> gives the corresponding temperature <math alttext="h"><mi>h</mi>
</math>, in degrees Fahrenheit, of any substance that has a temperature of <math alttext="v"><mi>v</mi>
</math> kelvins, where <math alttext="v greater than 0"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If a substance has a temperature of <math alttext="467.33"><mn>467.33</mn>
</math> degrees Fahrenheit, what is the corresponding temperature, in kelvins, of this substance?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["515"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["515"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="515"><mn>515</mn></math>. It’s given that the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math> gives the corresponding temperature <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math>, in degrees Fahrenheit, of any substance that has a temperature of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="v"><mi>v</mi></math> kelvins, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="v greater than 0"><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.&nbsp;Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="467.33"><mn>467.33</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math> in the given equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="467.33 equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32"><mn>467.33</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="32"><mn>32</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="435.33 equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction"><mn>435.33</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2,176.65 equals 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis"><mn>2,176.65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="241.85 equals v minus 273.15"><mn>241.85</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn></math>. Adding <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="273.15"><mn>273.15</mn></math> to both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="515 equals v"><mn>515</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></math>. Therefore, if a substance has a temperature of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="467.33"><mn>467.33</mn></math> degrees Fahrenheit, the corresponding temperature, in kelvins, of this substance is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="515"><mn>515</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"0bd33265","external_id":"e47cdf24-1ef9-4aa4-bc46-70b25da6e45e","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"ecefd45f-1ddd-40c3-8a90-fc78179dcee2","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.B.","skill_desc":"Linear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"h equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>273.15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math> gives the corresponding temperature <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math>, in degrees Fahrenheit, of any substance that has a temperature of <math alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi>\n</math> kelvins, where <math alttext=\"v greater than 0\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If a substance has a temperature of <math alttext=\"467.33\"><mn>467.33</mn>\n</math> degrees Fahrenheit, what is the corresponding temperature, in kelvins, of this substance?</p>","answerOptions":null,"keys":["515"],"correct_answer":["515"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"515\"><mn>515</mn></math>. It’s given that the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math> gives the corresponding temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, in degrees Fahrenheit, of any substance that has a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi></math> kelvins, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v greater than 0\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.&nbsp;Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"467.33\"><mn>467.33</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the given equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"467.33 equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32\"><mn>467.33</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math>.