":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"e47cdf24-1ef9-4aa4-bc46-70b25da6e45e","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"ecefd45f-1ddd-40c3-8a90-fc78179dcee2","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"h equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>273.15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math> gives the corresponding temperature <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math>, in degrees Fahrenheit, of any substance that has a temperature of <math alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi>\n</math> kelvins, where <math alttext=\"v greater than 0\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If a substance has a temperature of <math alttext=\"467.33\"><mn>467.33</mn>\n</math> degrees Fahrenheit, what is the corresponding temperature, in kelvins, of this substance?</p>","keys":["515"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"515\"><mn>515</mn></math>. It’s given that the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math> gives the corresponding temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math>, in degrees Fahrenheit, of any substance that has a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi></math> kelvins, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"v greater than 0\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.&nbsp;Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"467.33\"><mn>467.33</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the given equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"467.33 equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction plus 32\"><mn>467.33</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"32\"><mn>32</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"435.33 equals StartFraction 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis Over 5 EndFraction\"><mn>435.33</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,176.65 equals 9 left parenthesis v minus 273.15 right parenthesis\"><mn>2,176.65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"241.85 equals v minus 273.15\"><mn>241.85</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>273.15</mn></math>. Adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"273.15\"><mn>273.15</mn></math> to both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"515 equals v\"><mn>515</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></math>. Therefore, if a substance has a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"467.33\"><mn>467.33</mn></math> degrees Fahrenheit, the corresponding temperature, in kelvins, of this substance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"515\"><mn>515</mn></math>.</p>","externalid":"e47cdf24-1ef9-4aa4-bc46-70b25da6e45e","correct_answer":["515"]},"createDate":1755117017725,"updateDate":1755117017725}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017725, 1755117017725),
    ($SATQ$0c541d87$SATQ$, $SATQ$c470d4b9-a5d3-44e7-9e33-d10b5151dcde$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Systems of two linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Two customers purchased the same kind of bread and eggs at a store. The first customer paid <math alttext="12.45"><mn>12.45</mn>
</math> dollars for <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> loaf of bread and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> dozen eggs. The second customer paid <math alttext="19.42"><mn>19.42</mn>
</math> dollars for <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> loaves of bread and <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> dozen eggs. What is the cost, in dollars, of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> dozen eggs?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c16f7cfa-e87e-45db-9330-173a6d2fad5c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3.77\"><mn>3.77</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"bf4f5a63-6324-420a-9c1f-4531f2326ec6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3.88\"><mn>3.88</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ab69979-9aa5-44f1-8d28-4d8255607595","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4.15\"><mn>4.15</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f1a6f9f6-9033-4a09-b5d9-0bf9a50e3f0a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4.34\"><mn>4.34</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f1a6f9f6-9033-4a09-b5d9-0bf9a50e3f0a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Let <math alttext="l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> represent the cost, in dollars, of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> loaf of bread, and let <math alttext="d"><mi>d</mi>
</math> represent the cost, in dollars, of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> dozen eggs. It&rsquo;s given that the first customer paid <math alttext="12.45"><mn>12.45</mn>
</math> dollars for <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> loaf of bread and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> dozen eggs. Therefore, the first customer&rsquo;s purchase can be represented by the equation <math alttext="l plus 2 d equals 12.45"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.45</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the second customer paid <math alttext="19.42"><mn>19.42</mn>
</math> dollars for <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> loaves of bread and <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> dozen eggs. Therefore, the second customer&rsquo;s purchase can be represented by the equation <math alttext="4 l plus d equals 19.42"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19.42</mn></math>. The equations <math alttext="l plus 2 d equals 12.45"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.45</mn></math> and <math alttext="4 l plus d equals 19.42"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19.42</mn></math> form a system of linear equations, which can be solved by elimination to find the value of <math alttext="d"><mi>d</mi>
</math>. Multiplying the first equation in the system by <math alttext="negative 4"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="minus 4 l minus 8 d equals negative 49.8"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>49.8</mn></math>. Adding <math alttext="minus 4 l minus 8 d equals negative 49.8"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>49.8</mn></math> to the second equation, <math alttext="4 l plus d equals 19.42"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19.42</mn></math>, yields <math alttext="left parenthesis minus 4 l plus 4 l right parenthesis plus left parenthesis minus 8 d plus d right parenthesis equals left parenthesis negative 49.8 plus 19.42 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>49.8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>19.42</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="minus 7 d equals negative 30.38"><mrow>
