mn>\n</math>-sided polygon has one of three lengths. It's also given that the number of sides with length <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> <math alttext=\"centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis\"><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math> is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> times the number of sides <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> with length <math alttext=\"3 cm\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. Therefore, there are <math alttext=\"5 times n\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"5 n\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, sides with length <math alttext=\"8 cm\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. It&rsquo;s also given that there are <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> sides with length <math alttext=\"4 cm\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. Therefore, the number of <math alttext=\"3 cm\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, <math alttext=\"4 cm\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"8 cm\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math> sides are <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"5 n\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t<mi>n</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, respectively. Since there are a total of <math alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn>\n</math> sides, the equation <math alttext=\"n plus 6 plus 5 n equals 30\"><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math> represents this situation. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"6 n plus 6 equals 30\"><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math>. Therefore, the equation that must be true for the value of <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"6 n plus 6 equals 30\"><mn>6</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each side of a <math alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn>\n</math>-sided polygon has one of three lengths. The number of sides with length <math alttext=\"8 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math> is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> times the number of sides <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> with length <math alttext=\"3 cm\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. There are <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> sides with length <math alttext=\"4 cm\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. Which equation must be true for the value of <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>?</p>","externalid":"e2acc363-d0b7-4b19-ac43-34982f030a3d","templateid":"45d92f4a-4799-4c38-8729-b91c81c5a799","vaultid":"51b1ad54-6ba0-48e7-8b70-4e9e32a12f56","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"db684fea-f29b-4f1d-9f94-be7e86a767b1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5 n plus 6 equals 30\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>30</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c07e410d-e60d-47f8-afda-2a338b60a459","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 n plus 6 equals 30\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>n</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>30</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"007508ed-0fb2-4b88-ad11-ada45460ee11","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8 n plus 3 n plus 4 n equals 30\"><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"fde55bc2-5124-40c5-b72f-bf65bfd3f273","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8 left parenthesis 5 n right parenthesis plus 3 n plus 4 left parenthesis 6 right parenthesis equals 30\"><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959808,"updateDate":1691007959808}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959808, 1691007959808),
    ($SATQ$0d1b1e35$SATQ$, $SATQ$cd071339-36d3-4977-8ff2-863f8066f9ed$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A batch of banana milkshakes consists of <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> cups of ice cream and <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> bananas and has <math alttext="1,114 milligrams left parenthesis mg right parenthesis"><mn>1,114</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>milligrams</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>mg</mtext></mfenced></math> of calcium. There is <math alttext="276 mg"><mn>276</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mg</mtext></math> of calcium in <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> cup of the ice cream used to make this batch of milkshakes. How much calcium, <math alttext="in mg"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mg</mtext></math>, is in <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> banana?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d73a3655-f047-4315-b5cd-7c0349b9886d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4bc7159e-0254-4914-b787-45ebcc532e99","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"804c42da-cec5-4cac-8f6e-b32cb4aff9e3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"419\"><mn>419</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"de126fe7-ef41-4a42-994a-d73635fb7bcc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,104\"><mn>1,104</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d73a3655-f047-4315-b5cd-7c0349b9886d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It’s given that a batch of banana milkshakes consists of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> cups of ice cream and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> bananas and has <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,114"><mn>1,114</mn></math> mg of calcium. It’s also given that there is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="276"><mn>276</mn></math> mg of calcium in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> cup of the ice cream used to make this batch of milkshakes. It follows that the total amount of calcium in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> cups of ice cream is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4 left parenthesis 276 right parenthesis"><mn>4</mn><mo>⁢</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>276</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,104"><mn>1,104</mn></math> mg. Let <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> represent the amount of calcium, in mg, in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> banana. It follows that the total amount of calcium in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> bananas is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 x"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math> mg. Since the batch of banana milkshakes has <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,114"><mn>1,114</mn></math> mg of calcium, the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,104 plus 2 x equals 1,114"><mn>1,104</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,114</mn></math> represents this situation. Subtracting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,104"><mn>1,104</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 x equals 10"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 5"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Therefore, the amount of calcium in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> banana is&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5"><mn>5</mn></math> mg.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the amount of calcium, in mg, in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> bananas, not in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> banana.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the amount of calcium, in mg, in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="4"><mn>4</mn></math> cups of ice cream, not in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> banana.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"0d1b1e35","external_id":"cd071339-36d3-4977-8ff2-863f8066f9ed","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"859097af-5564-4d6a-991f-f4f2338e2255","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A batch of banana milkshakes consists of <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> cups of ice cream and <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> bananas and has <math alttext=\"1,114 milligrams left parenthesis mg right parenthesis\"><mn>1,114</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>milligrams</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>mg</mtext></mfenced></math> of calcium. There is <math alttext=\"276 mg\"><mn>276</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mg</mtext></math> of calcium in <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> cup of the ice cream used to make this batch of milkshakes. How much calcium, <math alttext=\"in mg\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mg</mtext></math>, is in <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> banana?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d73a3655-f047-4315-b5cd-7c0349b9886d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4bc7159e-0254-4914-b787-45ebcc532e99","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"804c42da-cec5-4cac-8f6e-b32cb4aff9e3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"419\"><mn>419</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"de126fe7-ef41-4a42-994a-d73635fb7bcc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,104\"><mn>1,104</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["d73a3655-f0